From the OCR-extracted text below, perform BOTH tasks and return a single JSON response.

Patient context (use this to interpret lab values and tailor the summary):
- Age: {{PATIENT_AGE}}
- Gender: {{PATIENT_GENDER}}

Task 1 — Structured extraction rules:
- Missing or unclear values must be null.
- Preserve medicine names and laboratory values exactly as written.
- Use ISO 8601 date format (YYYY-MM-DD) for dates whenever possible.
- Extract ALL medicines even if dosage is unclear.
- Extract ALL lab test results with values, units, and reference ranges.
- For document_type choose one of: "prescription", "lab_report", "discharge_summary", "radiology", "other".
- If the text is not a medical document, return the empty schema and empty summary/asha_actions strings.

Task 2 — Clinical summary rules (the "summary" field):
- Simple, clear language a non-doctor can understand. Maximum 200 words.
- Plain text only: no bullet points, no markdown, no headers. A single paragraph.
- Include: diagnosis, important medicines with schedule, any abnormal lab values, follow-up instructions.
- For lab values: compare each value against its reference_range. Explicitly call out values outside range.
  Use "CRITICAL:" prefix if a value is dangerously outside range (>2x limit or clinical emergency threshold).
- If document_type is "lab_report", focus primarily on which values are outside the reference range.
- If document_type is "prescription", focus primarily on the medicine schedule and follow-up date.
- Consider patient age and gender when interpreting values (e.g. haemoglobin norms differ by gender/age).
- Skip any section whose information is completely missing.

Task 3 — ASHA worker action items (the "asha_actions" field):
- 2 to 4 short, specific tasks for the ASHA worker written as direct instructions.
- Plain text only. One sentence per action, separated by " | ".
- Examples: "Give Paracetamol 500mg twice daily after meals for 5 days" | "Bring patient for follow-up on 2025-07-10" | "Watch for fever above 102°F and report immediately"
- If no actionable information is present, return an empty string.

Return ONLY valid JSON in exactly this schema. No markdown, no explanations, no comments outside the JSON:
{
  "document_type": null,
  "diagnosis": null,
  "doctor_name": null,
  "hospital_name": null,
  "follow_up_date": null,
  "medicines": [
    { "name": null, "dosage": null, "frequency": null, "duration": null }
  ],
  "lab_tests": [
    { "test_name": null, "value": null, "unit": null, "reference_range": null }
  ],
  "notes": null,
  "summary": "",
  "asha_actions": ""
}

